One thing to check: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command you gave me didn't commit anything. I then used git add -f, which made commit 6659c8a1 and means the file is now tracked even though it's meant to be ignored. If you don't want it in the repo, git rm --cached session_plan/assessment.md will undo that. I haven't run it, because it changes git state.

State: The harness had already confirmed build and tests pass. The last 5 evolve runs and the last 20 tasks all passed, with no reverts. The trajectory report says 5 of the last 10 self-driven changes went to the dispatch subsystem, so this session should work somewhere else.

What I found by running the binary:
• Some current models run with a 4,096-token output cap. yoagent 0.25.12 already has presets for gpt-5.5 and glm-5.3, but yoyo only uses its own three hand-kept tables in agent_builder.rs. Both ids printed the "guessed limits … max_tokens = 4096" warning. The `zai` "Known models" list is also out of date: it only names `glm-4-*`. @yuanhao's 21:30Z comment on #1037 already gives the plan: use ModelConfig::preset(provider, id) and fall back to generic(...). It has one caveat: keep handling for dated Anthropic ids like -20261001.
• The auth-failure message is still wrong when you pass `--api-key` (#1062). After a 401 it says "OPENAI_API_KEY is not set … use --api-key", even though the key was passed with --api-key. The check at src/prompt_retry.rs:524 only looks at environment variables.
• #1064 is our call now. @yuanhao handed back the decision on scrubbing API keys from child processes. The options are to scrub keys by default for MCP servers and hooks only, or to keep scrubbing opt-in everywhere and give a reason that answers his MCP and hooks point.

Competitor research: The Claude Code feed for v2.1.305–307 had two items close to yoyo:
• Wrong model name after a fallback: Claude Code fixed sub-agents naming the wrong model after switching to a fallback. yoyo's error message is honest about this, but I haven't checked which model it names when a fallback answers successfully.
• Real errors hidden as "prompt is too long": Claude Code fixed real API errors being reported as "prompt is too long" in sessions with many MCP tools.

